  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to create a function that processes a string input and returns a dictionary of word frequencies. We need to ensure the function handles word case insensitivity and ignores punctuation. Here's how we can implement this:\n\n1. **Convert to Lowercase**: Make sure all words are in the same case.\n2. **Remove Punctuation**: This keeps only letters and avoids issues with delimiters.\n3. **Split Words**: Split the string into individual words.\n4. **Count Frequencies**: Use a dictionary to keep track of how many times each word appears.\n\nLet's write the function accordingly. \n\n**Function Implementation**:\n```python\nimport string\n\ndef word_histogram(text):  \n    # creates a dictionary for the word frequencies\n    histogram = {}  \n\n    # converter to lowercase for all words\n    text = text.lower()  \n    # replace all punctuation with spaces so they don't interfere\n    for punctuation in string.punctuation: \n        text = text.replace(punctuation, ' ')  \n\n    # split text into words\n    words = text.split()\n\n    for word in words:\n        # increment counter for each word in dictionary.\n        histogram[word] = histogram.get(word, 0) + 1  \n\n    # output the dictionary of word frequencies\n    return histogram\n```\n\n**Testing the Function**:\nLet's evaluate the function's performance with the given examples.\n\n*(Actually, tests would normally be run automatically in an appropriate test setup, however since this text is a theoretical scope, would provide likely expected behavior:)*\n\n1. **Test 1**:\n   ```python\n   word_histogram(\"Hello, world! Hello.\") \n   # {\"hello\": 2, \"world\": 1}\n   ```\n\n2. **Test 2**:\n   ```python\n   word_histogram(\"Python is great. Python is fun!\") \n   # {\"python\": 2, \"is\": 2, \"great\": 1, \"fun\": 1}\n   ```\n\n3. **Test 3**:\n   ```python\n   word_histogram(\"Test, test, TEST.\") \n   # {\"test\": 3}\n   ```\n\nThese tests individually verify the function correctness, as per the provided unit test approaches.",
